                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which office handles 12A registration in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>12A registration for Mumbai-based entities is processed by the Principal Commissioner of Income Tax (Exemptions) at Aayakar Bhavan, M.K. Road, Churchgate, Mumbai 400020. The application is filed online through incometax.gov.in using Form 10A. Hearings and physical document submissions are conducted at the PCIT office. Patron's Marine Lines office is walking distance away.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the cost of 12A registration in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>There is no government fee for filing Form 10A. Through Patron, 12A registration starts from Rs 7,999 all-inclusive. The 12A + 80G bundled package is Rs 12,999. Additional charges for DSC procurement if needed (Rs 1,500-2,500). All fees exclusive of GST at 18%.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does 12A registration take in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>12A registration typically takes 30 to 60 days from Form 10A filing. This includes document preparation (3-5 days), Form 10A filing (2-3 days), and PCIT (Exemptions) Mumbai processing (15-45 days). Processing time varies based on PCIT workload and whether queries or hearings are needed.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is 12A registration mandatory for trusts in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes, if the trust wants income tax exemption on surplus income. Without 12A, the entire income - from donations, grants, investments, programme fees - is taxable. All Mumbai trusts registered with the Charity Commissioner must separately apply for 12A with the PCIT (Exemptions).</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a society and trust both get 12A registration?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Any non-profit entity - trust under BPT Act or Indian Trusts Act, society under the Societies Registration Act 1860, or Section 8 company under the Companies Act 2013 - is eligible, provided objects are charitable or religious. Private and family trusts are excluded.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if 12A registration is not renewed before expiry?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Under the post-2021 regime, 12AB is valid for 5 years. Renewal via Form 10AB must be filed at least 6 months before expiry. If missed, registration lapses and entire income becomes taxable from the following assessment year. The entity must then apply for fresh registration.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is 12A needed for CSR funding in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. CSR-1 registration on the MCA portal requires a valid 12A certificate. Mumbai corporates at BKC and Nariman Point directing CSR funds will not partner with NGOs lacking 12A. Additionally, 80G enables donors to claim tax deductions. Patron ensures 12A, 80G, and CSR-1 are all in place.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can 12A and 80G be applied together?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Both are applied through Form 10A on incometax.gov.in and processed by the same PCIT (Exemptions) Mumbai. Many Mumbai NGOs file both simultaneously. Patron offers a bundled 12A + 80G package at Rs 12,999 covering both applications, document preparation, and PCIT coordination.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


